                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "96405324-d7d8-47dd-b46b-15973289bb02",
                                "sense_id": "4470020a-123b-322a-8806-4e940eb29638",
                                "text": "No economist, with the possible exception of the most doctrinaire metallists, have ever expressed any other opinion. --American Economic Review (1938) 28, p. 316"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b351fb77-b935-4eb6-8025-d0d176032f93",
                                "sense_id": "4470020a-123b-322a-8806-4e940eb29638",
                                "text": "While not all Jacksonians were Metallists, or vice versa, the Jacksonian Metallists sought to purge the currency of small bank notes and replace them with gold and silver coins. --Exploring Economic History (1974) 11, p. 228"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5571be38-7df2-4aed-9556-8c8b9ecc7fe5",
                                "sense_id": "4470020a-123b-322a-8806-4e940eb29638",
                                "text": "The authors argue that Ricardo, unlike Marx, was no ‘metallist’, that is, he never applied the labour theory of value to the monetary metal to determine the general price level. --Economic Journal (1991) 101, p. 407"
                            }
                        ]
